Id: ssh023w
Severity: WARN
Category: ssh
Check: check_ssh
Fix: Set GatewayPorts no (the default).
References: sshd_config(5); CIS Ubuntu Linux 24.04 LTS Benchmark v2.0.0, 5.1.8 (Ensure sshd DisableForwarding is enabled)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-17, IA-2; ISO 8.5, 8.20; CE Secure configuration, User access control

GatewayPorts is yes or clientspecified: a remote port forwarding a user
sets up (ssh -R) binds to every interface of this host instead of
loopback, so any host that can reach this one reaches whatever the user
forwarded, typically a service on their own machine or network, with
no authentication from sshd on the way. The default is no, which is
what every distribution ships; clientspecified lets each client
choose, which is yes for the client that asks. Set it back to no, or
allow it in a Match block for the accounts meant to publish a service.
